flexdef/misc: make lerrsf_fatal variadic

lerrsf_fatal() is defined in misc.c and used by filter.c and scanflags.c,
but flexdef.h never declared it.  Declaring it with the K&R signature
(const char *, const char *) does not work either: scanflags.c calls it
with a long ("%ld of stack") while filter.c calls it with a string
("%s failed"), so a declaration must be variadic.

- add the missing prototype to flexdef.h (GCC 14 errors on implicit
  declarations);
- rewrite the K&R definition as an ANSI variadic function that formats
  with vsnprintf(), which is what the old code did semantically (it
  forwarded its single argument straight to the variadic snprintf()).
  K&R definitions cannot take "...", hence the ANSI form.

Signed-off-by: jeep <jeep@local>

--- flex-2.5.37.orig/flexdef.h	2012-07-23 08:27:24.000000000 +0800
+++ flex-2.5.37/flexdef.h	2026-10-01 21:49:42.228722563 +0800
@@ -908,6 +908,11 @@
 /* Report an error message formatted with one string argument. */
 extern void lerrsf PROTO ((const char *, const char *));
 
+/* Report a fatal error message formatted like a printf() format, and
+ * terminate.  Variadic: callers pass either a string (filter.c) or a
+ * long (scanflags.c), matching the format directives. */
+extern void lerrsf_fatal PROTO ((const char *, ...));
+
 /* Spit out a "#line" statement. */
 extern void line_directive_out PROTO ((FILE *, int));
 
--- flex-2.5.37.orig/misc.c	2012-07-23 08:27:24.000000000 +0800
+++ flex-2.5.37/misc.c	2026-10-01 21:49:42.228813481 +0800
@@ -411,12 +411,14 @@
 
 /* lerrsf_fatal - as lerrsf, but call flexfatal */
 
-void lerrsf_fatal (msg, arg)
-	const char *msg, arg[];
+void lerrsf_fatal (const char *msg, ...)
 {
 	char    errmsg[MAXLINE];
+	va_list ap;
 
-	snprintf (errmsg, sizeof(errmsg)-1, msg, arg);
+	va_start (ap, msg);
+	vsnprintf (errmsg, sizeof(errmsg)-1, msg, ap);
+	va_end (ap);
 	errmsg[sizeof(errmsg)-1] = 0; /* ensure NULL termination */
 	flexfatal (errmsg);
 }
